# ── Claude Code internal state ────────────────────────────────────
.claude/worktrees/
# Per-machine permission grants. This one is NOT shared: it accumulates
# whatever the person at this keyboard clicked 'allow' on, and this repo is
# public. .claude/settings.json (no .local) is the shared one.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json.bak

# ── Large media binaries (keep marketing video/audio out of git) ──
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.avi
*.mkv
*.wav
*.mp3

# Local nightly-automation secrets & logs
.claude-gh-token
.claude-gh-token.txt
Business Plan/files/Night Tasks/logs/

# ── Internal analytics working notes (local only) ─────────────────
# ANALYTICS_CONTEXT.md is the brief read in full before any GA4 or Meta figure
# is computed. It is deliberately candid -- unfixed ad defects, conversion
# rates, which campaigns are failing, corrections to previously published
# numbers -- because its whole job is to stop the next analysis repeating the
# last one's mistakes. That candour is exactly what should not sit in a PUBLIC
# repo, and this one is public.
#
# It has never been tracked. These rules exist so a stray `git add -A` cannot
# change that, which is how stripe_backup_code.txt ended up readable for 103
# days. The glob is deliberately broader than the path: a copy saved elsewhere
# in the tree is the same disclosure.
#
# Analytics output meant for sharing goes in reports/ instead, where it is
# written knowing it will be public.
Business Plan/files/Night Tasks/ANALYTICS_CONTEXT.md
*ANALYTICS_CONTEXT*

# ── Untracked credential notes (NEVER commit) ─────────────────────
# These sit in Business Plan/files/ and hold real values, including
# META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKENS. They were never tracked -- these rules exist so a
# stray `git add -A` cannot make them public, which is exactly how
# stripe_backup_code.txt ended up readable for 103 days.
Business Plan/files/Environment Variables.txt
*Environment Variables*
*Set env vars*
*env_vars*
# ── Stripe 2FA recovery material ──────────────────────────────────
# This file sat in a PUBLIC repo from 2026-05-09 to 2026-08-21 (103 days).
# It is a two-step-authentication BACKUP CODE, not an API key -- rotating
# API keys does nothing about it; the codes must be regenerated in
# Dashboard -> Settings -> Your account -> Two-step authentication.
# Untracked rather than deleted so the local copy survives until then.
# NOTE: untracking does NOT remove it from git history.
Business Plan/files/stripe_backup_code.txt
*backup_code*

# ── Scraped venue contact data (NEVER commit) ─────────────────
# "Business Plan/SparkDate/" holds a 258-row CSV of real venue contact
# names, emails and phone numbers compiled from Google Places and from
# the venues' own websites. It was untracked but NOT ignored -- the same
# state stripe_backup_code.txt was in before it sat in this public repo
# for 103 days. Publishing a compiled contact list is a privacy problem
# even though the rows are business contacts rather than individuals.
# Enrichment output is written next to its input by scripts/scrape-venues.js,
# so the generated copies are covered here too.
Business Plan/SparkDate/
*sepa_bars*
*.enriched.csv

# ── content/ is a two-file directory, on purpose ──────────────────
# queue.csv and brand.json are the source of truth for the social calendar.
# Nothing else belongs here. Design source masters (31.5 MB of PNG) and the
# superseded worksheets were once pasted in, which would have put binaries
# git can never forget into a public repo -- and undone the point of moving
# the queue out of a folder full of near-identical copies.
#
# Deny-by-default so an accidental paste cannot be committed. To add a
# genuinely new file here, add a matching `!` line below.
content/*
!content/queue.csv
!content/brand.json
!content/README.md
# The registry of free event-listing surfaces, and the reasons the rejected
# ones were rejected. Source, not an export: scripts/build-listing-pack.js and
# .claude/commands/syndicate-events.md both read it.
!content/listing-sites.json
# The women-facing outreach registry -- local businesses and community groups,
# which are a different motion from the calendars above (a human, not a form).
# Source, not an export: scripts/build-outreach-pack.js and
# .claude/commands/women-outreach.md both read it.
!content/women-surfaces.json

# Source art and superseded exports live in OneDrive, not the repo:
#   OneDrive\SparkDate\SourceArt              <- the PNG masters
#   OneDrive\SparkDate\Superseded_2026-08-22  <- the dead worksheets
# Published JPEGs are committed at public/social/ -- those are the ones that
# actually publish, and they are ~2.5 MB rather than 31.5 MB.
*_SUPERSEDED_*/

# ── Generated analytics exports ───────────────────────────────────
# GA4 and Meta exports are dropped into Night Tasks by hand and by
# scripts/fetch-meta-insights.js, then read by the nightly review. They are
# inputs to a report, not source -- and they accumulate fast (19 sitting
# untracked when this was written).
Business Plan/files/Night Tasks/download*.csv
Business Plan/files/Night Tasks/data*.pdf
Business Plan/files/Night Tasks/*.csv

# ── Dormant duplicate ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The LIVE Night Tasks folder is "Business Plan/files/Night Tasks/". The bare
# one at the repo root is a leftover an older version of
# run-nightly-claude-code.ps1 pointed at by mistake; that script now carries a
# comment saying so. Ignored rather than deleted -- it still holds two old
# reports nobody has re-read.
/Night Tasks/

# Excel lock files -- created while a workbook is open, never source.
~$*
